// Kerbol, the star system of Kerbal Space Program, in place of 82 Eridani
// (sector 1,-1, next to Sol). Loaded by src/custom_system.c.
//
// Scaled up to real size with one rule: distances and radii x10, masses x100
// (that keeps each body's surface gravity: Kerbin comes out 6000 km, 0.89
// Earth masses, 1 g, 0.91 AU from a 0.88-sun star). KSP figures from memory,
// loosely; orbital phases are KSP's mean longitudes, roughly.
// Exceptions: Mun moved out to 360000 km (x30, about our Moon's distance, so it
// looks Moon-sized) and Minmus to 650000 km (x14, kept inside half Kerbin's
// Hill sphere of ~1.36M km).
// Spin: the scaling makes orbits ~3.2x (sqrt 10) slower than KSP, so days are
// stretched the same way (Kerbin 6 h -> ~19 h); spin 1 (24 h) is the nearest
// step for every rotating body. Moho and the locked moons stay 0.
//
//
// See docs/system-overlays.md for the format.
